Scheme: Saksham Yuva Scheme
Question: What are the criterion to allocate honorary assignment to the approved applicant under the scheme?
Answer: Honorary assignments will be offered seniority-wise and the seniority of the applicants shall be determined as per the following criteria:-
i) Firstly, the applicant with higher age, as per the list, shall be higher in seniority;
ii) In case the age is same, then the applicant who has obtained the 10+2/graduate/post-graduate degree earlier, shall be senior (for this the year of successful completion of 10+2/graduate/post-graduate studies shall be considered);

Scheme: Saksham Yuva Scheme
Question: Is there any penalty for not reporting on honorary assignment?
Answer: If 10+2/graduate/post-graduate qualified Saksham Yuva who fails to attend to/report to any honorary assignment he/she is nominated for within 3 days then:-
a) In the first instance, if he/she fails to report within 7 days, then the unemployment allowance shall be discontinued and his/her name shall be kept in abeyance/debar from the list of beneficiaries for one month;
b) In the second instance, if he/she fails to report within 7 days, then the unemployment allowance shall be discontinued and his/her name shall be kept in abeyance/debar from the list of beneficiaries for one year;

